== an invalid KOSHCONF names the reason:
warning: The KOSHCONF environment variable is ignored because it is not padded standard base64.
-c:1:15: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The value is not a valid KOSHCONF encoding: it is not padded standard base64.
warning: The KOSHCONF environment variable is ignored because a record is truncated.
-c:1:15: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The value is not a valid KOSHCONF encoding: a record is truncated.
warning: The KOSHCONF environment variable is ignored because a varint is not in its shortest form.
-c:1:15: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The value is not a valid KOSHCONF encoding: a varint is not in its shortest form.
warning: The KOSHCONF environment variable is ignored because its option ids are out of order.
-c:1:15: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The value is not a valid KOSHCONF encoding: its option ids are out of order.
== a Bash name points at its koshconf name:
-c:1:14: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Unknown option 'pipefail'.
note: 'pipefail' is the Bash name of 'interpreter.posix.pipeline_fails_on_any_stage'.
-c:1:37: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Unknown option 'extglob'.
note: 'extglob' is the Bash name of 'interpreter.bash.glob_extended_patterns'.
== a retired set -o name points at its replacement:
-c:1:8: error: Builtin `set`: Unknown -o option 'koshkit'.
note: The option was retired; use `koshconf set interpreter.resolve_koshkit_applets_as_commands on` instead.
-c:1:24: error: Builtin `set`: Unknown -o option 'no-diagnostics'.
note: The option was retired; use `koshconf set optimizer.analyze_before_running on` instead.
-c:1:47: error: Builtin `set`: Unknown -o option 'no-unset'.
note: The option was retired; use `set -o nounset` instead.
-c:2:8: error: Builtin `set`: Unknown -o option 'failglob'.
note: The option was retired; use `shopt -u failglob` instead.
== an invalid init_moods names the bad entry:
-c:1:25: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Unknown mood 'fish' in the value of 'init_moods', expected a comma-separated list of 'kosh', 'sh', 'bash', and 'bash-posix'.
== enumeration values read naturally:
-c:1:31: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Invalid value 'ed' for 'editor.base_mode', expected 'emacs' or 'vi'.
-c:2:56: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Invalid value 'true' for 'completion.add_space_after_completed_word', expected 'off', 'on', or 'on-excluding-trailing-slash'.
# Insert a space after an accepted completion: off for never, on for always, or
# on-excluding-trailing-slash for all but a directory.
--
# Color the input by syntax and suggest the rest of the word in ghost text. Both
# also need completion.on_tab on.
